@title Metroid - Zero Mission (USA)
@file Metroid - Zero Mission (U) [!].gba
@game BMXE
@chip SRAM
@status wip: reaches Samus standing in the first Brinstar room on a new Normal file. Starting the file writes only the header/select-slot blocks (no Samus data: file A still reads --:--:--), so the first real save needs Samus to reach the first save station in Brinstar (platforming through several rooms). A human should record: file A, Start Game, Normal, play to the first save room, stand on the station and answer Yes, quit after "Save complete". [load]: file A shows Brinstar and the play time; Start Game resumes in the save room.

# Intro > title (PRESS START) > SAMUS DATA > file A > Start Game > Normal >
# intro text > Brinstar.

[new]
wait 600
press START
until text "ZERO MISSI" timeout=600 every=10
wait 60
checkpoint title
press START
until text "SAMUS DATA" timeout=600 every=10
wait 60
checkpoint samus_data
press A
until text "Start Game" timeout=300 every=5
wait 60
press A
until text "Difficulty" timeout=300 every=5
wait 30
checkpoint difficulty
press A
until text "Planet Zebes" timeout=900 every=10
mash A until notext "Zebes" timeout=1200 every=20
wait 600
checkpoint brinstar window=10
